Module imbar_things "The things of Imbar's stories" {
  // What more than one adventure hands on, finds or asks after: clues and tokens that go from one story to another (the
  // Imbar author's cross-adventure gifts), not kinds of thing a dungeon is drawn with. The catalog (data/catalog/items/)
  // holds only the kinds there are; these are the canon's, as the College and the House of Doors are, and every
  // world and campaign has them before any adventure names one (the owner, 6 November).
  Kind pharos_rubbing "A rubbing of the Prefect's table" is treasure worth 8 described "A long strip of rag paper rubbed black with charcoal, taken from a table of bronze in the lamp room of the Pharos on Skerrow: columns of Aenean numerals, and beside them, in a second column that was scrubbed and never quite cleared, a series of strokes that are not Aenean. The rubbing is faithful, and says nothing of what it means.".
  Kind pharos_lens "The green lens of a Pharos" is treasure worth 40 described "A lens of green glass the width of a dinner plate, in an iron ring, heavy as a sleeping child. Round its rim are twelve settings for small stones; eleven hold a pale stone each, and the twelfth is an empty socket, bright, as if something had been taken out of it not long ago or a very long time ago. On the iron ring, cut small: a fish, and over it a flame.".
  Kind prefects_writ "A copy of a Prefect's writ of keeping" is treasure worth 10 described "A monk's copy, in a clerkly hand, of a writ of the Prefect of the Marches giving a House the keeping of a wall it did not build: CUSTODIA, NON DOMINIUM. The Latin is plain. The reading of it has been disputed for eight hundred years.".
  Kind tally_rubbing "A rubbing of a keeper's tally" is treasure worth 8 described "A wax-and-cloth rubbing of the underside of a stone bench, three notations deep: a long stroke for a ship, short ones under it, a flame cut into some, a paw into others; the oldest rows in marks no one reads, the middle in Aenean numerals, the last in an island's own. It is a bilingual, of a kind: the numerals gloss the strokes.".
  Kind collegium_letter "A letter of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments" is treasure worth 5 described "A folded letter in a cramped, delighted hand, bearing the seal of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments at Corran: the bearer is a friend of the Collegium and of working things, and is to be admitted where the Collegium's name opens doors, which is fewer places than the Collegium believes.".
  Kind surety_terms "The Ninth Valuer's note on a surety" is treasure worth 6 described "A strip of ruled paper in a hand like type: A SURETY ANSWERS FOR THE KEEPING NAMED. WHERE NO KEEPING IS NAMED, FOR ALL. Under it, a small exact mark where a name would be, and the word RECEIVED.".
  Kind watch_tally "A Watch's tally-stick" is treasure worth 3 described "A stick of grey wood the length of a forearm, cut with eleven close notches and a space for a twelfth. It is warm to the hand. It was cut by someone who has not been asked, in a very long time, for anything.".
  Kind lamplighter_seal "Lamplighters' seal" is gear worth 10 described "A brass seal on a chain, a lamp with a hand closed round it: the Charter's mark, which the old doors of the Lamplighters still answer to.".
  Kind sluice_rod "Notched rod" is tool worth 1 described "A staff of black wood shod at both ends in bronze, the bronze notched along its edge in a close, careful pattern.".
}
